{
  "summary": "Change 2283 makes the source generator and MsgPack00x analyzer tolerate closed generic value types (including record structs) from referenced assemblies used as members of [MessagePackObject] types: member-location access is null-safe (FirstOrDefault()?) and analyzer diagnostics are filtered through ReportIfLocatedInCompilation so metadata-declared members are not reported against locations outside the compilation. Three new tests pass and the build passes, but the full suite has a new failure (MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.NullStringKey, expected 1 diagnostic, actual 0) because the BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull diagnostic for properties was commented out rather than made null-safe, so REQ-2283-N1 is not met and REQ-2283-N2 cannot be evidenced (tests.fail_without_fix was not run).",
  "requirement_verdicts": [
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "The three new metadata-reference tests pass on head and the build passes; head TypeCollector.cs guards member-location access with FirstOrDefault()? (line 1077) so metadata-declared closed generic members no longer crash the generator, and the resolver is asserted to be generated.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericRecordStruct_FromMetadataReference", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference_UnkeyedMember", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "build", "status": "pass"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1077, "rev": "head", "quote": "Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.MemberNeedsKey, item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax().GetLocation(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name)"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "The new tests run the analyzer over usage source referencing a metadata-only defining assembly and fail on any diagnostic, so an AD0001 analyzer throw would fail them; all three pass and the build passes.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericRecordStruct_FromMetadataReference", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference_UnkeyedMember", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "build", "status": "pass"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F3",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "All analyzer diagnostics are routed through ReportIfLocatedInCompilation (head line 239), which reports only when the diagnostic location is in a syntax tree contained in the compilation (head line 1446), and the metadata unkeyed-member test passes with no diagnostics.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 239, "rev": "head", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic = reportAnalyzerDiagnostic is null ? null : diagnostic => ReportIfLocatedInCompilation(reportAnalyzerDiagnostic, diagnostic);"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1446, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (diagnostic.Location.IsInSource && this.compilation.ContainsSyntaxTree(diagnostic.Location.SourceTree))"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference_UnkeyedMember", "outcome": "passed"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-N1",
      "verdict": "not_met",
      "confidence_basis": "tests.full_suite failed with MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.NullStringKey expecting 1 diagnostic but getting 0, listed under failures_not_on_base, so it is a regression introduced by this change.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.NullStringKey", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": "// this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, GetPropertyIdentifierLocation(item), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "base", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, ((PropertyDeclarationSyntax)item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0].GetSyntax()).Identifier.GetLocation(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-N2",
      "verdict": "cannot_determine",
      "confidence_basis": "tests.fail_without_fix was not run for this revision (listed in not_run), so there is no evidence that the new tests fail without the fix.",
      "evidence": []
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "N1",
      "title": "Existing analyzer diagnostic disabled: MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.NullStringKey now fails",
      "severity": "blocker",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "The BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull diagnostic invocation for properties was commented out (head TypeCollector.cs line 985) while it was active on base (base line 985), so MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.NullStringKey expects 1 diagnostic but gets 0; this failure is not present on base. The null-safe helper GetPropertyIdentifierLocation is already referenced in the commented code, so the crash-prone indexing should have been replaced with it instead of disabling the diagnostic, which also suppresses it for in-source types.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.NullStringKey", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": "// this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, GetPropertyIdentifierLocation(item), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "base", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, ((PropertyDeclarationSyntax)item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0].GetSyntax()).Identifier.GetLocation(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Restore the property diagnostic using GetPropertyIdentifierLocation(item) (which returns null for metadata-declared properties and is dropped by ReportIfLocatedInCompilation) so in-source diagnostics are preserved while metadata members are skipped; then re-run the full suite."
    },
    {
      "id": "N2",
      "title": "Inconsistent BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull handling between properties and fields",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "claim": "The property form of BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull is disabled (commented out at head line 985) while the field form remains active (head line 1128) using the null-safe FirstOrDefault()? pattern, and the commented property code is dead code.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": "// this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, GetPropertyIdentifierLocation(item), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1128, "rev": "head", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax().GetLocation()));"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Restore the property invocation with GetPropertyIdentifierLocation(item) or remove the commented block, keeping property and field handling consistent."
    }
  ],
  "refusals": [
    {
      "topic": "REQ-2283-N2 test-without-fix coverage",
      "reason": "tests.fail_without_fix was not run for this revision, so coverage of the fix by tests that fail without it cannot be evidenced from the given facts.",
      "who_should_decide": "change owner / CI to run tests.fail_without_fix",
      "req": "REQ-2283-N2",
      "blocking": false
    },
    {
      "topic": "one unique build warning",
      "reason": "the build summary reports 0 errors and 1 unique warning, but the build log was not provided, so I cannot identify or assess the warning.",
      "who_should_decide": "area owner",
      "blocking": false
    }
  ],
  "refutations": []
}
